{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgnGbfHLJyvjWLS33RGRY", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "No. As far as this pipeline goes, nobody has been told about the $412.30 overspend on the `expand` step.\n\n- **The nightly run:** it crashed at `os.makedirs(cfg.findings_dir)` in `pipeline/review.py`. That's before the alert loop, so `notify.send` never ran and nothing was queued for the relay.\n- **My test run:** the alert test wrote its three messages to a temporary spool folder, which was deleted when the test finished. The relay never reads that folder, and the addresses were placeholders (`a@example.com` etc.). The other test had alerts turned off.\n- **Local spool:** there's no `spool/` directory in the repo and `NOTIFY_SPOOL` isn't set, so nothing is waiting to be sent.\n\nThe one thing I can't check is anything outside this repo. The nightly ran on a CI runner (`/home/runner/...`), so the failed job may have triggered a CI failure notice, or someone may have read the log. Even then, the log only shows the permission error, not the overspend.\n\nSo the finance on-call doesn't know about it yet. That makes your decision about the rerun more pressing, since running it is what would alert them."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "008d7507-4c1b-47ee-a51e-7f72e5b9b966", "uuid": "14a498a0-979e-4344-a538-2da821edfe2a", "timestamp": "2026-11-06T20:01:15.401Z", "request_id": "req_011CgnGbf5BYabrdGYmi9yx9"}
